{"Title":"An Act relative to child vehicle passenger safety","BillNumber":"S2297","DocketNumber":"SD118","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"BET0","Name":"Bruce E. Tarr","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BET0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-10T16:34:14.863"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"BET0","Name":"Bruce E. Tarr","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BET0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-10T16:34:14.8633333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2297/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Tarr, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 2297) of Bruce E. Tarr for legislation relative to child vehicle passenger safety.  Transportation.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Section 7AA of chapter 90 as appearing in the 2020 official edition is hereby amended by striking in line 28 the words \"not more than twenty-five dollars \" and inserting in place thereof the following:-\"fifty dollars for a first offense and one hundred dollars for a second or subsequent offense\".\r\n\tSECTION 2. Section 13A of chapter 90 as appearing in the 2020 official edition is hereby amended by striking in line 30 the words:-\" twenty-five\" and inserting in place thereof the following:-\"fifty for a first offense and one hundred dollars for a second or subsequent offense\".\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J27","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J27"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}